अक्ष् (perhaps a kind of old Desid. of √ 1. अश्) cl. 1. 5. अक्षति, अक्ष्णोति (Pāṇ. iii, 1, 75; fut. अक्षिष्यति or अक्ष्यति, L.; aor. आक्षीत्, 3. du. आक्षिष्टाम् or आष्टाम्, L.; perf. आनक्ष [Pāṇ. vii, 4, 60 Comm.], but Ā. p. [with the Vedic weak stem आक्ष् cf. perf. आश्-उः 3. pl. &c. fr. √ 1. अश्] आक्षाण॑),
to reach, RV. x, 22, 11;
to pass through, penetrate, pervade, embrace, L.;
to accumulate (to form the cube?), L. :
Caus. अक्षयति, आचिक्षत्, to cause to pervade, L. :
Desid. अचिक्षिषति or अचिक्षति, L.

आ-√ क्षि cl. 2. -क्षेति (3. pl. -क्षिय॑न्ति and impf. आ॑क्षियन्; Pot. 1. pl. -क्षियेम)
to abide, dwell in (acc.), inhabit, RV.; AV.;
 -क्षेति, to possess, take possession of (acc.), RV. : cl. 6. -क्षिय॑ति, to exist, AV. x, 5, 45.

अक्षीब and अक्षिब, mfn. not intoxicated, sober, L.
 m. Guilandina or Hyperanthera Moringa, L.;
 n. sea salt, L.

अक्षीब and अक्षिब, mfn. not intoxicated, sober, L.
 m. Guilandina or Hyperanthera Moringa, L.;
 n. sea salt, L.

आ-√ क्षिप् -क्षिपति (ind.p. -क्षिप्य) to throw down upon (loc.) or towards (dat.), MBh. &c.;
to strike with a bolt, R. vi, 78, 5;
to convulse, cause to tremble, Suśr.;
to draw or take off or away, withdraw from (abl.), MBh. &c.;
to chase or drive out of a place (abl.), disperse, MBh. iii, 539; BhP.;
to put into (loc.), Suśr.;
to point to, refer to, hint, indicate, Pāṇ. vi, 3, 34; Siddh.; Sāh. &c.;
to refuse, object to (acc.), MBh. iii, 16117; Kāvyād. &c.;
to insult, deride, Mn. iv, 141; MBh. &c.;
to excel so as to put to shame;
 (perf. -चिक्षेप) to challenge, call to a dispute &c. (dat.), Kathās. :
Caus. (perf. -क्षेपयाम् आस) to cause to throw down, MBh. iii, 15733.
